# Use case: will my product work on the Wi-Fi where it will be installed?
#
# Take the EVK to the spot where the product will sit and run this. It joins the network,
# watches the signal for 30 s, checks the way to the internet and gives a verdict with advice
# (EXCELLENT, GOOD, FAIR or POOR).
#
# You need: a NORA-W36 EVK, and the network name and password in the environment
# (the password never appears in the output or a report):
#   $env:UCX_WIFI_SSID = "MyNetwork"; $env:UCX_WIFI_PASS = "MyPassword"
#   .\ucxapp --script examples/use-cases/wifi-site-check.ucx --junit site.xml
dev.info
expect Model:\s+NORA-W36
wifi.connect ${UCX_WIFI_SSID} ${UCX_WIFI_PASS}
wifi.survey 30
expect Verdict:\s+(EXCELLENT|GOOD|FAIR)
dev.diagnose
expect Result:\s+PASS
